{title: Til Jesus Is All}
{artist: Larry Holder}
{time: 4/4}
{key: F}
{tempo: 83}

Verse 1
[F]Thy Word I have hidden, [Dm]dear Lord, [Bb]in my heart,
[C]Seeking daily [Bb]to follow [C]Your Way,
[F7]But more [A]times [Bb]than I [C]count, I go [Am]off on my [Dm]own,
And I [Bb]find my heart going [Gm7]astray.
[C7]Oh, [F]I know that it [Dm]grieves You, as [Bb]Father to son:
[C]You want more than [Bb]I [C7]seek to achieve.
[F7]O [Bb]God, open my [C7]heart, [C]help my [Am]will to [Am7]let [Dm]go,
Help my [Bb]staggering faith [Gm]to [Gm7]believe!

Refrain
[C]Burn [C7]away [Fmaj7]all [F]the dross [Dm]I've collected [Bb]in vain,
[C]Take [C7]the [F]silver and gold, [Dm]and refine [Bb]it again.
[C]Turn [C7]my heart [Am]to Your own, clear [Dm]each sin [Gm]that You [Gm7]see,
[C]Til Jesus [Bb]is all [F]that is [Am]left [Gm]of me,
[C]Til Jesus [Bb]is all [F]that is left...

Verse 2
[C7]Thy [F]Word is a Lamp [Dm]and a Light [Bb]for my path,
[C]If [Bb]only I'll follow [C]it [C7]through.
[F7]It's [Bb]not that You [C]haven't [C7]provided [Am]the way,
[Dm]For [Dm7]You've shown [Bb]us the [Bbmaj7]Way [Gm]that is true.
[C]And [C7]sometimes [F]I am torn [Dm]'tween what's good [Bb]and what's best
[C]Just as much [Bb]as what's good [C]and what's [F]bad.
[F7]Turn Your light [Bb]on my soul, [C]search and [C7]try [Am]me today,
[Dm]Give [Dm7]me reason [Bb]to [Bbmaj7]sing [Gm]and be [G7]glad!
